#### Micro-Internship: Google Analytics 4 Setup for Nonprofit

Job Description
Project Description

Important: This project requires direct, hands on work inside Fresh Community Development Inc.’s actual Google Analytics 4, Google Search Console, Google Tag Manager, and website accounts for 2-3 small websites. You will be granted access to these accounts and are expected to perform setup, configuration, testing, and verification directly. This is not an audit only or recommendation only project.

Project Overview:

Audit, set up, and optimize digital measurement across 2-3 small websites. Ensure each site is properly connected to Google Analytics 4 and Google Search Console, that the most important user actions are being tracked, and that simple reporting views are available for ongoing performance monitoring. The final outcome should be a working, tested analytics system on each website, with agreed upon key events and conversions actively tracking and reporting correctly. Where technical barriers require developer intervention, document the issue clearly and provide specific, actionable instructions for our web developer.

Deliverables

1 to 2 slide executive summary highlighting what was implemented, key findings, and next steps.
Implementation report (maximum 3 pages):
For each website, summarize GA4 installation status, Search Console connection, Tag Manager setup where applicable, and event/conversion tracking before and after implementation.
Include a summary table showing the key actions being tracked, such as form submissions, registrations, contact clicks, calls to action, and other important user activity.
GA4, Search Console, and Tag Manager setup documentation (maximum 2 pages):
Briefly document how each platform was set up or corrected for each website.
Include screenshots where helpful.
Event and conversion configuration sheet (maximum 2 pages):
List the events and conversions configured for each website.
Explain how they were implemented through GA4, Google Tag Manager, or another appropriate method.
Confirm how each event or conversion was tested and verified.
Working dashboard or reporting views:
Create simple reporting views that allow the organization to monitor website traffic, traffic sources, top pages, user activity, and conversions.
The reporting should use the organization’s live analytics setup, not only sample or demo data.
Tracking verification:
Test the completed setup and confirm that agreed upon events and conversions are firing and appearing correctly in analytics reporting.
Identify and document any tracking that could not be fully completed.
Technical developer handoff (maximum 1 page):
For any issue requiring coding or developer assistance, clearly explain what needs to be changed, why it is needed, where the change should occur, and what result should be expected once completed.
Short written guide (maximum 1 page):
Explain how our team can review the analytics, understand the reports, and monitor key performance indicators going forward.
Recommendations for future measurement (maximum 1 page):
Identify opportunities to improve tracking, reporting, attribution, or future marketing analysis.
Source sheet (maximum 1 page):
Include links to relevant Google documentation or other resources referenced during the project.
AI Disclosure Form (maximum 1 page):
If AI was used to assist with any part of the project, briefly explain how it was used.
Notes

You will be expected to work directly inside our live GA4, Google Search Console, Google Tag Manager, and website accounts as needed for the sites.
The goal is to implement and verify the analytics system, not simply evaluate it or provide recommendations.
Do not require or use internal, private, or proprietary information outside of the accounts and access specifically provided for this project.
The 2-3 websites are small organizational, program, technology related websites that may include forms, contact pages, calls to action, registrations, and other measurable user activity.
Advanced custom website development is not required. If custom coding is necessary, document the requirement clearly for our web developer.
Focus on hands on implementation, accurate tracking, testing, simple reporting, and clear documentation.
Company Description

We are a community based nonprofit organization committed to strengthening foundations for housing security and financial stability through practical financial education and business development support. We help families move from survival mode to growth mode by creating clear pathways toward stable housing, homeownership, and long term asset ownership. We are a 501(c)(3) organization dedicated to serving the working low to moderate income families by providing practical, cost effective resources that strengthen financial and business literacy and create clear pathways to long term housing stability and homeownership in Florida, Georgia, and Michigan.

